{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Let it not be evil in your eyes, etc. — all that Sarah says to you.</b> Let it not be evil in your eyes — what she says concerning the boy and the maid-servant, to expel them with marks of servitude, as he said: <b>upon her shoulder, etc.</b>" "<b>Listen to her voice.</b> For she is right to do thus." "<b>For in Isaac shall seed be called to you.</b> And Ishmael and his sons shall be servants to him — for in Isaac shall seed be called to you, and not in him."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The lemma cited as עַל שִׁכְמָהּ ('upon her shoulder') does not correspond to Genesis 21; likely an indirect reference to Genesis 16:6 (ותשם על שכם שפחתה) or a similar passage about servitude. The exact referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:00.599515687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}